WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:18.820
Blantyre at Earlshall until Lady Anne recovered from her fall.

2
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.541
Then he returned home.

3
00:00:22.161 --> 00:00:25.702
The head groom, Reuben Smith, drove him to the train since Mr.

4
00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:27.402
York was still in London with the earl.

5
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:33.484
The cart needed some repairs, so Reuben had decided to leave it in town.

6
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:36.874
He'd brought along a saddle to ride me home.

7
00:00:38.135 --> 00:00:40.737
First he left me at the hotel stable to eat and rest.

8
00:00:42.218 --> 00:00:44.480
The grooms had me ready to leave again at four o'clock.

9
00:00:46.722 --> 00:00:47.903
But Reuben wasn't ready yet.

10
00:00:48.403 --> 00:00:50.605
He was having a fine time drinking at the pub.

11
00:00:52.086 --> 00:00:54.368
He didn't show up until almost nine o'clock.

12
00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:59.492
As soon as he climbed into the saddle, I could feel that something wasn't right.

13
00:01:00.873 --> 00:01:03.576
Reuben was normally an excellent rider with a light hand.

14
00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.665
Now he swayed back and forth and yanked at the reins.

15
00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:12.668
As we left town, he kicked me into a gallop.

16
00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:19.831
I obeyed, even though I could feel one of my shoes coming loose and it was a little

17
00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:22.312
uncomfortable. "Faster, you!"

18
00:01:22.692 --> 00:01:24.633
he shouted, smacking me with his whip.

19
00:01:25.194 --> 00:01:27.775
"Faster!" I didn't understand.

20
00:01:27.795 --> 00:01:30.096
I was already going as fast as I could!

21
00:01:30.984 --> 00:01:34.505
My muscles strained, and my shoe loosened more with every stride.

22
00:01:36.466 --> 00:01:39.627
It was a dark night, and I could hardly see where I was going.

23
00:01:40.687 --> 00:01:44.428
That made it impossible to avoid uneven or rocky spots on the road.

24
00:01:45.528 --> 00:01:48.569
We reached a place where the road workers had laid some new stone.

25
00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.890
That was when my loose shoe finally came off.

26
00:01:54.591 --> 00:01:57.692
Galloping over the stones on my tender foot was very painful.

27
00:01:58.908 --> 00:02:02.970
I started to slow down, but Reuben struck me again with the whip, so I kept going.

28
00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.132
My hoof started to crack as the stones dug into my foot.

29
00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:11.414
No horse could keep going forever under such conditions!

30
00:02:11.874 --> 00:02:12.794
But I did my best.

31
00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:17.257
Finally my bare foot hit a slippery patch of gravel.

32
00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:21.078
I stumbled and lurched forward, landing hard on both knees.

33
00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.540
Reuben was flung out of the saddle and hit the ground.

34
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.122
I climbed to my feet and limped off to a softer spot.

35
00:02:31.164 --> 00:02:34.647
My knees hurt, my foot was sore, and I was exhausted.

36
00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:40.672
I waited for Reuben to get up, but after a few groans, he lay silent and still.

37
00:02:41.753 --> 00:02:42.573
And so I waited.

38
00:02:43.894 --> 00:02:48.358
The moon rose, and I could see the empty road stretching away in both directions.

39
00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.661
Hours passed before I heard a cart approaching.

40
00:02:54.543 --> 00:02:58.262
As it came nearer, I thought I recognized the sound of Ginger's step.

41
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:03.607
Sure enough she soon came into view pulling two men in a small cart.

42
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:07.070
The men soon spotted me—and Reuben.

43
00:03:09.492 --> 00:03:11.894
It turned out that Reuben had been killed in the fall.

44
00:03:13.315 --> 00:03:17.719
I wasn't blamed for the accident, as it was easy enough for everyone to figure out what had

45
00:03:17.779 --> 00:03:24.837
happened. One of the men led me carefully back to Earlshall Park, where the grooms tended to my

46
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:26.939
injured knees and wrapped my sore foot.

47
00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.761
The foot healed quickly.

48
00:03:30.762 --> 00:03:32.264
My knees were another story.

49
00:03:32.284 --> 00:03:37.628
"I don't think the joint is injured," the veterinarian told the grooms.

50
00:03:37.648 --> 00:03:42.532
"This horse should be able to return to full work after a while.

51
00:03:43.613 --> 00:03:46.255
But he'll always have ugly scars on his knees."

52
00:03:46.275 --> 00:03:49.878
"That's too bad," one of the grooms said.

53
00:03:49.898 --> 00:03:51.600
"The lady won't like that."

54
00:03:53.396 --> 00:03:57.378
It took a long time for my knees to heal, with lots of painful treatments.

55
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.422
After some time in my stall, the grooms put me out into a small pasture.

56
00:04:06.003 --> 00:04:08.444
I spent a month or so grazing and resting out there.

57
00:04:09.145 --> 00:04:11.546
It was nice, although I was a little lonely.

58
00:04:13.507 --> 00:04:14.828
One day I heard the gate open.

59
00:04:15.548 --> 00:04:19.110
When I looked over, I saw a groom releasing Ginger into the field!

60
00:04:20.331 --> 00:04:22.472
I trotted over to her with a joyful whinny.

61
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.021
She was glad to see me too.

62
00:04:26.062 --> 00:04:28.544
But her reason for being there was not a happy one.

63
00:04:30.025 --> 00:04:33.108
She told me the earl's son had been riding her too hard lately.

64
00:04:34.309 --> 00:04:38.972
During a hunt, he'd pressed her so much that she'd ended up with a strained back and breathing

65
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:43.356
problems. "We are not quite the horses we once were, are we?"

66
00:04:43.736 --> 00:04:44.617
she said sadly.

67
00:04:46.378 --> 00:04:48.320
Still we were happy to be together again.

68
00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:53.084
We enjoyed the next few weeks until the earl finally returned from London.

69
00:04:56.076 --> 00:04:57.437
He and York came to see us.

70
00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.138
The earl frowned as he looked us over.

71
00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:03.240
"What a waste of good horses!"

72
00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.281
he told York.

73
00:05:04.301 --> 00:05:10.584
"I feel terrible, especially since I told my friend that these two would have a good home here."

74
00:05:10.604 --> 00:05:16.447
"Ginger, the mare, might come around after a rest," York said.

75
00:05:17.468 --> 00:05:18.329
The earl nodded.

76
00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:20.610
"We'll give her a chance," he said.

77
00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.192
"But I can't have a horse with those knees in my stables.

78
00:05:24.865 --> 00:05:26.230
The black one will have to be sold."
